WEBVTT

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.450
Nanami-senpai.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.330
Yuu. Good morning.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.290
Good morning.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.120
Were you able to sleep? Are you okay?

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.910
Huh? Yeah.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.250
Let's do our best for the last day of the study camp.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:17.330
Komorebi kirakira yureteru asa no

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.200
Namikimichi

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:30.790
Itsumo no kimi no "ohayou" tte koe ga kikoeru

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.500
Kagi o kaketa glass no hako ni

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:42.500
Nani o kakushite irundarou?

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:48.750
Ugokihajimeta monogatari

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.370
Kimi no sekai motto shiritakute

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:59.500
Guuzen fureta sono yubi o

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.080
Ima nigittanda

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.540
Tsuyogari mo yowasa mo

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:14.080
Zenbu tsutsunde ageru yo

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:20.120
Gyutto

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.120
Sis! Don't you think this is a good chance
for us to be a real family?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.450
You need to speak with more a gentle tone in this scene.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.620
Sis... don't-

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.660
If you just lower your voice, then the audience
isn't going to be able to hear you!

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.250
Huh? Then how should I do it?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.200
This is why I keep telling you all,
enunciation is important!

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.330
...you don't seem very similar to Mio at all.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.250
You were the ideal girl that everyone looked up to.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.620
Can a person really be that perfect?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.750
Maybe I was just desperate to appear
that way to everyone at school?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.160
The sister I knew at home must have been the real one.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.250
What reason could you have to pretend
to be so cold and lonely?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:18.370
I wonder. Maybe by removing myself,
you and my parents made a more harmonious family.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.660
Isn't it possible I was just fulfilling
the role you all wanted of me?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.790
In front of me you always exposed your weakness,
along with everything else.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.870
Showing weakness doesn't necessarily
guarantee it was the real me, right?

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:37.500
It's possible I simply made you believe that it was,
because you were happy to have me rely on you.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.330
Who else is there?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.910
Besides these three, there could be more people
who knew a totally different "me".

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.540
...don't seem very similar to Mio...

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.790
Everyone I knew saw me wearing a different mask,
and no one really knows who I was underneath them!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.080
And now I'll never know!

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:01.700
Whoa...

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.370
If that's the case...

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.450
I have to pick one of those masks
and believe that it's real.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.830
I can only choose one of them to adopt
for the rest of my life.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.500
It's about time we took a break, no?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.620
Yeah... you're right.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.500
Touko...

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.330
Huh?

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.410
Want a sip?

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.160
Thanks.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.950
I'm going to the convenience store,
is there anything you want?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.830
Where will you spend your
summer vacation?

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.620
What happened with Nanami-senpai earlier? Is she okay?

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.580
What type of riceballs did Dojima-kun say he wanted?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.830
Saeki-senpai!

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.580
Spicy
Pollock
Roe

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.540
It's okay.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.290
She may seem like she's struggling,
but I think this will be good for Touko in the end.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.000
I don't think Touko wants any of
the first-years worrying about her, frankly.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.620
I'm already watching out for her.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.080
Let's go.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.830
Would you like me to buy you some ice cream?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.040
No thank you!

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:27.290
Something I said to you recently was the same
as what "I" said in the past, right?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.410
So, I feel that I can trus-

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.950
That's not bad, but it doesn't feel quite as emotional
as your performance from this morning.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.910
Okay.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:41.250
You should read through the second-half
of the script one more time.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.040
Right.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.580
Are you still thinking about changing the ending?

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.040
No, I think this is good.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.450
It's fine.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:06:00.250
Out of the three versions of herself,
she ultimately choses the one who was with her lover.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.370
The personality that she showed to
the person who she chose to love,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.790
must be the real version of herself.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:11.750
But...

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.750
We might get stage fright up here.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.910
You think?

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.120
Looking from up here,
there's a lot more room than expected.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:25.370
We can only use it while the sports clubs
are on break, so don't waste any time.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.120
I can barely hear you!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.660
Huh? Seriously?

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:37.040
Okay! Let's go ahead and have everyone
practice on projecting their voices!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:37.750
Go!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.910
Awaiting the sensation of a short, sharp, shock,

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.080
from a cheap and chippy chopper on a big black block.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:55.080
Maybe there's some messages or
pictures left on your smartphone?

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.290
Maybe, but... it's locked and needs a password.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:00.700
See?

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.620
Without some sort of a hint, I guess
you'll have a hard time getting it unlocked.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:12.540
I've been checking, making sure I didn't write
a note or keep something on me that would help.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.660
But nothing yet...

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.700
Well, it hasn't been long since you regained
consciousness, so don't rush it.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.540
I have an idea.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:27.250
How about you try asking the people who
know you about the memories they have of you?

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.080
I would rather die...

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:47.870
Huh?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.500
Only this day is circled for some reason,
but nothing is written. What could it have been?

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.950
October 10th...

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.370
Maybe that was...!

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.580
It unlocked!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.540
I started to think about becoming
a replacement for my sister.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.200
Is that... really necessary?

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:15.160
Even now, I still want the same thing.
Just to be by your side.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.080
I won't expect anything from you.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.040
You can go on just as you are!
I only want to be the one who stays next to you.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.910
Is that not enough?

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.950
Right now, I'm hardly even a person.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:37.000
I have to choose who I want to be from here on out,
yet I had no idea how I should go about doing that.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:44.870
But something I said to you recently was
the same as what "I" said in the past, right?

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.000
So, I feel that I can trust the "me"
that was together with you!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.330
I want to believe in her.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:57.370
The person I was when we were together,
that was the real me.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.830
I'm still not very confident about all of this, but...

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.700
...will you stay together with me, like before?

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.370
Yes, of course.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.620
Thank you.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.290
Shall we take a walk outside?

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.160
Yes, let's.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.330
I almost forgot.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:24.160
Um, do you have any idea what
the day of October 10th represents?

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:29.000
Huh? That's my birthday, but... how did you know that?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.040
Oh really?

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.540
What?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.410
It's a secret.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.040
No way, tell me!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.410
You all did a great job over the past three days.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.830
It's shaping up to be quite the show,
so I'm excited for the culture festival.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.410
Until you resume practice next semester,
make sure you all keep doing those vocal exercises!

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.000
Don't forget your summer homework.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.830
Yes ma'am...

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.370
Okay, Nanami-san?

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:05.120
Right. Ichigaya-san, Hakozaki-sensei, thank you
very much for your time over the past three days.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:10.540
Thanks to you, we were able to improve a lot
during practice. Thank you very much!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.540
Thank you very much!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.080
Catch ya later!

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.250
He's quick!

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.950
Nanami-senpai.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.250
Let's go home together.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.500
So, are you going on any trips over summer vacation?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:44.160
Let's see... I think we'll visit the town
my father grew up in during the Obon Festival.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.660
Other than that, nowhere special. How about you?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.410
My family's plans are pretty similar to yours.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:53.450
What should we do?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:55.370
Let's wait.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.000
Well, see you later!

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.250
Senpai.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.000
Would you like to come over to my house?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:58.950
Huh?

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.370
Don't you want to spend time in my room again?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:11.580
I'll pass. We just finished the study camp
and you must be tired, so...

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.750
What are you so afraid of?

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:19.870
Are you still worried that I might end up
hating you or something?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.370
We made a promise, didn't we?

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:29.370
I'm staying by your side and helping out with the
stage show. I haven't fallen for anyone else, either!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:32.870
My feelings towards you haven't become hate nor love!

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:35.040
I'm keeping up my end of the deal!

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.700
So please have a little more faith in me, Senpai!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:45.700
If we just say our goodbyes here, then we won't see
each other for a while and I don't want that.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.250
If we go to your room now...

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:52.250
Huh?

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:57.700
I think... I'm going to really indulge myself with you...

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:01.450
...is that okay?

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:08.910
Suddenly Suffocating

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.500
I don't mind.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.950
Suddenly Suffocating

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.500
Fujishiro
Bookstore

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.080
What's wrong?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.330
It's nothing.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.660
Oh, it was hot in here. I'm sorry.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.450
Would you like a popsicle?

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.580
Yuu...

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.080
Sit over here.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.290
Like this?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.160
The popsicles are going to melt.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.580
Which do you want, orange or grape?

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.500
Grape, I guess.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.790
You can eat it by yourself.

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.120
What?

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.410
When you said you were going to indulge yourself,
this isn't exactly what I expected.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:45.370
Oh yeah? Did you start having lewd thoughts?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.620
No, not really...

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.660
I sure did.

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:28.500
Your lips are cold.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:55.040
So, it turns out that Ichigaya-san was a classmate
of my sister's and used to be on the Student Council.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:55.910
Yeah?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:16:00.160
I asked him what my sister
used to be like when she was at school.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.870
From what he told me, she was
a totally different person from who I knew...

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:15.950
Do you think that if I asked someone else,
they might have known her differently, too?

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:23.910
I think the same is true for everyone,
more or less. Don't you?

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:28.000
Although the main character in our show
is kind of an extreme example.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.750
But if that's true...

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:35.120
...then I don't know who I should strive to be anymore.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.660
Do you really have to "become" someone?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:44.870
I do.

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:54.500
What reason is there for me to stay the way that I am?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.370
Senpai, you...

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:24.910
Yuu...

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:32.080
Don't fall in love with me, okay?

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.160
Yeah, I know.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:50.500
Okay.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:55.450
Because, you know, I hate myself.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:18:01.870
And I can't be in love with someone
who likes the things I hate, right?

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.000
I want to keep loving you.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.870
Then you should do the same...

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.700
This is far enough. Bye for now.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.000
You should do the same...

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:53.040
...don't tell me you hate the things that I like!

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:50.500
You idiot!

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:58.580
Senpai, you idiot!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.700
Tomi Station

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:15.330
Yuu? What's going on?

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:17.540
Sorry, do you have a minute?

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.330
Yeah.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.290
Well, I wanted to talk to you about
the ending of the show.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.500
Yeah?

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:27.830
Let's do something else.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:28.750
Huh?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:33.620
Something other than the main character having
to choose between her three personalities.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.120
Will you consider writing a different ending?

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:39.910
It might be arrogant of me.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.790
In fact, Senpai may not even
want things to turn out this way.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:45.950
No...

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.080
She definitely doesn't.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.250
But, even so.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.660
Let's change it.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.580
You just got back from study camp, didn't you?

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:01.290
I'll be right back!

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.080
I...

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:08.200
...want Nanami-senpai to learn to stop hating herself!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.750
That may just be my selfish wish...

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:15.750
...but even so!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:20.540
I want for her...!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.250
I want Nanami-senpai to...!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:33.540
Sorry. It's not because I think the ending
we have now is bad or anything. It's just...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.950
I gathered that much already. It's fine.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:42.120
To be honest I was still hesitant myself,
I thought there must be a better way to end it.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:43.830
Right.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:47.450
But why did you decide that you wanted to change it?

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.040
Well...

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:57.830
The main character believes that among her three
personalities, one of them must be the real her, right?

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:02.450
She is hung up on the idea that
there's a single answer that she has to find.

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:09.660
So, she searches through her diaries, her mail,
and even questions all her visitors.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.580
And the answer she finds in the end
is to be with her lover.

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:17.410
But if you think about it, that's not really
the will of her current self, is it?

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:24.040
She's using the standards set by her past self
in order to decide, not what she currently believes.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:31.290
From start to finish, the only character the audience
knows is the current version of her on the stage.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:36.160
They never see what the character is
actually like with her memories.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:41.790
Despite that, the ending uses
the past version of her as its base...

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:49.790
...which makes it seem like the period of time
during the show is totally meaningless.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.200
I get it...

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.330
That's what was bothering me this whole time!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.160
You're right.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:02.750
The main character should make her decision based on
what she gets out of that time in the hospital.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:09.040
However, like you said, her decision in this ending
is based on nothing but what happened in the past.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:18.000
Thanks, Yuu. I think I finally figured out
why I was never satisfied with the ending.

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:22.410
Your face looks way more scary than grateful...

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:28.410
I'm grateful, but it's frustrating! I wanted
to figure out what needed to be fixed on my own!

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:31.080
I don't have time to be worried about
how I look right now!

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:32.700
Just wait a second.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:38.200
Okay. Let's rewrite it.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:39.540
Really?

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:43.580
I know I'm the one who asked you,
but that's a lot of effort to put in

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:47.290
and I can't say for sure whether
everyone else will approve or not.

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:49.080
I know.

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:53.200
Still, if there's a chance I can make it better,
then I'm going to write.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:55.160
Thanks.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:57.790
But hey, Yuu?

00:22:57.790 --> 00:22:58.620
Huh?

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:03.200
What made you start thinking about it all at this point?

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:08.000
It just kind of came to me... I guess.

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:14.750
Actually, it's probably because I want to make a change.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.120
No matter if it's arrogant, or selfish of me.

